# 026 · Ship v0.1.0

**Status:** `READY` · **Version:** [v0.1.0](../roadmap.md#v010) · **Part:** The release · **Depends on:** [001](001-plans-in-public.goal), [002](002-ci-and-repository-settings.goal), [003](003-advisors-no-default-cap.goal), [004](004-secret-scan.goal), [005](005-sample-project.goal), [007](007-known-limits.goal), [008](008-community-files.goal), [009](009-subscription-sign-in-tests.goal), [010](010-published-images.goal), [011](011-release-bundle.goal), [012](012-version-checks.goal), [013](013-thermite-doctor.goal), [014](014-quick-start-in-ci.goal), [015](015-log-paging.goal), [016](016-small-fixes.goal), [017](017-legacy-names.goal), [018](018-runpod-spike.goal), [019](019-rig-only-entry.goal), [020](020-runpod-rig-image.goal), [021](021-enrollment-codes.goal), [022](022-runpod-launch.goal), [023](023-runpod-lifecycle.goal), [024](024-runpod-models-and-results.goal), [025](025-runpod-tests-and-docs.goal), [060](060-docs-site.goal), [062](062-research-folder.goal), [063](063-scan-and-steer.goal), [064](064-experiment-queue.goal), [065](065-journals-and-corpus.goal), [066](066-direction-rules.goal), [067](067-assign-queue-from.goal), [068](068-mcp-servers-for-agents.goal)

## What

When every other v0.1.0 goal is verified:

1. Test the quick start on clean machines, from the release bundle and from source: Linux with Docker, macOS with Docker Desktop, and macOS with Podman.
2. Run the full checks and the acceptance suites the release touches, once.
3. Open a pull request into `main`. Merge it when CI passes.
4. Write the changelog.
5. Tag `v0.1.0`. The tag publishes the images.
6. Publish the GitHub Release, with notes on what works, the known limits and how to report a bug.

## Why

This is the first release that people outside the project can install and test.

## Done when

- [ ] `main` holds the release, and the tag and the images exist.
- [ ] The release notes are published.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-19, owner: The first public release is v0.1.0. It holds the tester basics, published images and rigs on RunPod.
- 2026-10-19, owner: The code moves to `main` only as the last step before the release.

## Open questions

- How the code reaches `main`: a pull request merged as a fast-forward (recommended), or a squash into one commit.

## Progress

- 2026-10-19: Goal written from the v0.1.0 release plan.
- 2026-10-20: Depends on every v0.1.0 goal in the release plan, goals 001, 060 and 062 to 068 included; goal 006 was dropped into 060.

